From b1db9e1c0918a3160cf3ac4ef59346803adb4780 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exploitizm <351399878+exploitizm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:25:51 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] radv/ps5: mesh shaders of emulated task draws run as compute
 (slice 1)

The PS5's NGG mesh launch (GFX10.1 in GS mode) deadlocks primitive assembly
and the shader exporter (the klog: PA, SX and SPI busy, GE and SC idle), in
a way that depends on what ran before: a meshlet that passes in one chunk
hangs in a later one, and one mesh workgroup alone in its own draw, the GPU
idle before and after, can hang (Ocarina of Time, about 40 console runs).

A graphics pipeline with a task and a mesh shader (an emulated task shader,
radv_task_emulated) now runs its mesh shader as compute, as radv_gs_compute
runs a geometry shader NGG cannot (radv_mesh_compute.c):

- radv_graphics_shaders_compile splits the mesh stage: the mesh shader,
  its outputs and SetMeshOutputs lowered to stores into a slot per mesh
  workgroup (radv_device.mesh_compute_bo), its workgroup ID, grid, draw ID
  and task payload read from its record, becomes a compute pass; the
  pipeline's hardware vertex shader becomes a copy that reads the slots and
  draws 3 vertices a primitive slot, a triangle list (an unused slot three
  equal corners);
- per emulated task chunk, after the task shader, the records prepass
  writes a record per mesh workgroup and the compute pass's workgroup count
  and the copy's vertex count (mode 4), then the compute pass runs, then the
  copy draws.

First slice: direct draws, triangles, positions and generic varyings, no
per-primitive outputs but the indices, no multiview, monolithic pipelines;
others keep the hardware path. Behind /data/eglantineps5/radv-mesh-compute.txt
(1) until it is proved.
